    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nAs part of adding a feature to `cython-lint`, I need to start parsing .pxd files, not just .pyx.\n\nHowever, the `parse_from_strings` usage fails for some .pxd because of of the syntax for default values:\n\n```\n...\nCython.Compiler.Errors.CompileError: \nError compiling Cython file:\n------------------------------------------------------------\n...\n\ncdef void simultaneous_sort(\n    floating* values,\n    intp_t* indices,\n    intp_t n,\n    bint use_three_way_partition=*,\n                                  ^\n------------------------------------------------------------\nsklearn/utils/_sorting.pxd:9:34: Expected an identifier or literal\n```\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```cython\nfrom Cython.Compiler.TreeFragment import parse_from_strings, StringParseContext\nfrom Cython.Compiler.Errors import init_thread\n\ninit_thread()\nfilename = 'sklearn/utils/_sorting.pxd'\nwith open(filename) as fd:\n    code = fd.read()\ncontext = StringParseContext(filename)\ncontext.set_language_level(3)\ntree = parse_from_strings(filename, code, context=context)\nprint(tree)\n```\n\nWhere the file being parsed is https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/blob/e67ae2f1412a4c67ce4c24061ce44af2af3d5bcb/sklearn/utils/_sorting.pxd\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nParse the file successfully.\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.2.8\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-21T08:27:31Z",
