        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think that this might just be a case of adding\n\n```\nscanner.parse_comments = False\n```\n\nto\n\nhttps://github.com/cython/cython/blob/9ffda81e7358e58e2c6fff16d4d2d40772565e66/Cython/Compiler/TreeFragment.py#L86-L87\n\n(which would obviously require a small change to Cython). The first thing we do when scanning a module is the look for `# cython: ...` type directives, and then turn comment parsing off. Setting `level` manually skips that bit though\n\n\n",
